    "skyPreset": "golden_alpine_meadow",
    "loreSummary": "Broken rock down the whole western side of this region and sand over the rest of it. The longest rock spine drawn anywhere runs the west; the east carries a salt floor, a stone pavement and a single ridge of sand nearly twenty kilometres long, lying over one another. No road comes onto it and nobody lives on it, so everything is carried in and everything is carried out, and a party works one side or the other and leaves the rest alone for the season."
  },
